                                        <div class="ielts-reading-question-section-content">
                                            <div class="ielts-reading-section-content-wrapper"><p>Complete the notes below.</p>
<p>Choose <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> from the passage for each answer.</p>
<p><em>Write your answers in boxes on your answer sheet.</em></p>
<p class="ielts-reading-passage-subhead"><strong><strong>Silbo Gomero</strong></strong></p>
<p><strong>How Silbo is produced</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>high- and low-frequency tones represent different sounds in Spanish <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">20</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="20" name="question_20" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[20] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span></li>
<li>pitch of whistle is controlled using silbador’s <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">21</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="21" name="question_21" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[21] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span></li>
